;;; Commentary:

;; `llm-review' is a production-ready Emacs package providing a Magit-style
;; code review interface for findings generated by Large Language Model (LLM)
;; coding assistants and external static analysis tools.
;;
;; Key features:
;; - Uses `magit-section' as the UI engine for collapsible code snippet previews.
;; - Converts LLM findings (file paths, start_line, end_line) into live Emacs
;;   buffer markers (`make-marker' with insertion type `t').  This prevents
;;   line-number drift as edits or deletions occur elsewhere in the source buffers.
;; - Defines `llm-review-mode' derived from `magit-section-mode' with intuitive
;;   single-key bindings:
;;     - TAB: Toggle code snippet preview (`magit-section-toggle')
;;     - d: Delete the target code block in the source buffer, clean up markers,
;;          and refresh the UI.
;;     - x: Dismiss the finding without modifying the source file.
;;     - RET: Jump to the exact source location (`llm-review-visit').
;;     - n / p: Navigate to next/previous finding.
;;     - g: Refresh the review buffer with dynamically updated line numbers.
;; - Ingests JSON arrays of findings generated by external CLI tools via
;;   `llm-review-load-file'.

;;; Code:

(require 'cl-lib)
(require 'json)
(require 'magit-section)
(require 'pulse nil t)
(require 'subr-x)

